codex
Added **39 CLI tests** in [call-chain.test.ts](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/code_map/test/a2/call-chain.test.ts), with four fixture projects—three using Effect services. Updated the [progress file](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261014-code-map-build/nodes/a2-tests.progress.md). Source and earlier tests are unchanged.

**33 pass; 6 fail.** I wrote these checks; their results cover these fixtures only.

Below, names omit the common `A2` prefix and `— Fails if: "…"` suffix. Unmarked tests pass.

**“a known place is not found”**

- exact service code locates its place
- description over a comment locates its place
- description over a string locates its place
- inline generator code locates the body holding the call
- a line inside a service body is a known place

**“an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate not built is not named”**

- ambiguous exact code lists every place
- ambiguous description lists every place
- ambiguous name in where lists every place
- ambiguous name in callers lists every place
- ambiguous name in callees lists every place
- ambiguous name in chain lists every place

**“a known link within the depth is missing with no limit at its site naming why”**

- defaults to six call links each way through services
- honors independent caller and callee depths
- setting only up preserves the other default
- setting only down preserves the other default
- level zero excludes every call link
- callers only keeps the enabled direction
- callees only keeps the enabled direction
- **FAIL:** service shortest callee route from launchDetourFirst preserves its tail
- service shortest callee route from launchShortcutFirst preserves its tail
- **FAIL:** service shortest caller route preserves its tail
- **FAIL:** direct shortest up route preserves its tail
- **FAIL:** direct shortest down route preserves its tail
- entering an inline Effect body adds no callee level
- **FAIL:** leaving an inline Effect body adds no caller level
- a dynamic callback may stop with an explanation at its site
- **FAIL:** every computed service call has its own dynamic limit

My reading of the failures:

| Failing test | Why it fails |
|---|---|
| Service shortest callee route, detour first | First reaches `sharedDispatch` at level 3, then suppresses its links when reached at level 1. |
| Service shortest caller route | First reaches `receiveShared` by the longer route, hiding callers within the shorter route’s depth. |
| Direct shortest up route | Omits `receiveSeal → receiveRecord`, which belongs at level 3. |
| Direct shortest down route | Omits `recordInspection → sealInspection`, which belongs at level 3. |
| Leaving an inline Effect body | Omits `inspectFromDoor → inspectParcel`; the caller walk stops at the anonymous body. |
| Every computed service call | Reports a dynamic limit for the first call only; the second site has neither a link nor its own limit. |

**“a shown link contradicts the code”**—the other clause of the same failure condition:

- shown service links agree with source in both directions — also covers missing links
- a stored function reference is not a caller

**“a link lacks its kind or location”**

- service links in both directions give kind and locations
- direct and constructor links give kind and locations

**“a function reached twice is shown twice”**

- diamond callees show the shared function once with a reference back
- diamond callers show the shared caller once with a reference back
- repeated call sites keep both links and one expansion
- inspectSelf up returns a reference to level zero
- inspectSelf down returns a reference to level zero
- inspectCycle up returns a reference to level zero
- inspectCycle down returns a reference to level zero
- repeated service target names where it was shown

Last lines of `bun test test/a2` (exit 1):

